# A task handed over with `panel` (the mock model's "in a panel"): an agent
# panel opens beside the delegating one, the focus staying where it was, and
# follows the task; once it is over the panel holds the delegate's session,
# its report in sight, and the report goes back to the delegating agent too.
size 160x40
config side-models.toml
mock-llm
start
wait "README.md"
key Alt+A
wait "Agent"
key Alt+Home Alt+F11
type "delegate the stock scan in a panel"
key Enter
wait "I'll hand the stock scan to a subagent in a panel." 20
wait "Agent wants to run start_session" 15
type "1"
wait-gone "Agent wants to run start_session" 10
# The panel following it: its input names whose delegate it is.
wait "Agent: SUBTASK: list the items" 10
wait "Delegate of default" 5
snapshot following
# The focus stayed in the delegating panel: what is typed goes there (the
# panel following the task takes no input).
type "zzfocuscheck"
wait "zzfocuscheck" 5
# Over: the panel holds the delegate's session, its report among it, and
# the delegating agent quotes the same report.
wait "SUBREPORT: 3 items under their" 30
# Open to go on with: the input asks for the user's words.
wait-gone "Delegate of default" 10
wait "The subagent is back: 3 items, checked on qwen3-coder-subagent" 30
snapshot done
quit
